Quoting @sebkrier
I think a particularly important skill is actually knowing when (and how) to use language models and when not to. Language models cheapen and reduce the barriers to producing a lot of text, and so it's easy to generate a lot and overwhelm people. Many people are already overflowing with information, it's not helpful to send them a ten page document you generated in less than an hour. Good to use models to help with conciseness and curating what you share/don't share. Many meetings could be emails, and many ten-pagers could be one page long.

