Excellent essay! Well worth reading.

@danshipper: "We’ve automated every single thing we can with AI agents. And yet there’s way more human work to do than ever. We’ve gone from 4 to 30 human employees since GPT-3. I wrote a report on the structural reasons: how AI makes expert competence cheap, why that drives up demand for experts, and why the dynamic only intensifies as we approach AGI."

AI progress creates more work for humans, not less.

