Interesting to see LLM councils being implemented for frontier models through skills and integrations. Previous research on council structure highlighted the importance of model diversity, suggesting that a council drawing from different foundation models would be more effective than one based solely on Claude. That research is outdated, and new experiments with the latest models are needed.

Thanks to @ATabarrok for flagging this and to @karpathy for developing the council idea. New research on council structure and efficacy will be started soon, so stay tuned.

